 3. 💡 Optimistic gift for young people 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 Cover: Authors Equity

 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Jim VandeHei calls this the most important book he'll ever write: It's aimed at giving college kids, young workers and all of us a different, more optimistic, actionable way to see and navigate our world.

 It started as a letter to the Axios CEO's kids , then became a full-fledged plan to maximize your mind, mood and career. "In a world that often makes you feel small and powerless," Jim writes, "the one thing you truly own is you. YOU own what you do, read, share, think, eat and spend your time on. This book shows you how to maximize that mentality. ... You've got this!" 🧀 What's next: Jim will launch an ask-me-anything college tour in January to talk about AI, politics, work, life and the best damn country in the world. 

 Stops include: Indiana, William Penn, Arkansas, Boston College, Stanford, UVA, South Carolina, University of Wisconsin-Oshkosh (Jim's alma mater, UWO!), Maine, Elon and Princeton. Please email our amazing tour maestro, Madeleine Woolgar, if you want your alma mater — or company — to be part of the mix. 

