 7. ☎️ Talkin&#x27; turkey 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 A screen with thawing and roasting times hangs at the front of the talk line call center. Photo: Carrie Shepherd/Axios Since 1981, the Butterball Turkey Talk-Line in Naperville, Ill., has answered millions of harried, frustrated and emotional calls (and now texts and chats) with urgent questions about cooking the turkey.

 The talk line opens at the beginning of November and runs through Christmas Eve every year. 🍗 The talk line started with six home economists on phones with Rolodexes of answers. Now it's about 60 people with earpieces and laptops.

 Everyone who works there has some food-related degree or training, including chefs, dietitians, food scientists and food stylists, reports Axios Chicago's Carrie Shepherd, who visited the call center this week. 🧊 The No. 1 query? "Some kind of thawing question," talk line supervisor Jessica Romanowski says.

 Others: "How do I thaw my turkey? ... How long will it take to thaw my turkey? ... Why isn't my turkey thawed yet? ... Oh no, I forgot to start thawing my turkey. How do I do it?" Thawing and carving tips . 

 
 
